## Root Cause

In the Wilson score interval formula, both the midpoint **and** the half-width must be divided by `den = 1 + z²/n`. The current code correctly divides `mid` by `den`, but **misses dividing `half` by `den`:

```go
// internal/eval/record.go:53 (buggy)
half := z * math.Sqrt(p*(1-p)/n+z*z/(4*n*n))  // ← missing /den!
```

For n=10, `p=0.5`, the missing `/den` adds ~0.26 to the width (a 1.38× overestimate), producing [0.14, 0.86] instead of the correct [0.24, 0.76].

The fix is straightforward — dividing `half` by `den`:

```go
// internal/eval/record.go:53 (fixed)
half := z * math.Sqrt(p*(1-p)/n+z*z/(4*n*n)) / den
```

